<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scheinfeld</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Scheinfeld is a small town in Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steigerwald">Steigerwald</a> hills. Above it stands Schwarzenberg Castle, from which the lords of Seinsheim took the name Schwarzenberg in the 15th century. The lands around Scheinfeld formed the core of the princely family's immediate territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scheinfeld.jpg" alt="Scheinfeld" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kassandro · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ScheinfeldOst.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
